<?php

namespace App\Services\ApiDocs\Docs;

/**
 * What each API module (first path segment, one OpenAPI tag) is for, written for
 * a reader that only has the OpenAPI document, such as another AI agent. Every
 * module of the document must have an entry and no entry may outlive its module
 * (ApiDocsDescriptionsTest). The listing endpoint of a module backed by a table
 * domain of the same name is appended by ApiModuleTagsTransformer.
 */
final class ApiModuleDescriptions
{
    /** @var array<string, string> */
    public const array DESCRIPTIONS = [
        'absence-allowances' => 'Absence allowances (Spettanze): the yearly entitlement of one person for one absence type (Tipi di assenza). Each one is keyed by user_id + absence_type_id + year and holds annual and carried-over minutes. PUT upserts one allowance and returns the refreshed balance row. The bulk endpoint sets many user_ids at once from a number of days, scaled to each person\'s daily minutes; null resets to the type default. Requires absence-requests.manageAll.',
        'absence-balances' => 'Absence balances (Saldi assenze): read-only figures computed per absence type and year: allowance, carry-over, accrued, used, pending and residual minutes. GET returns your own balances, or those of user_id if you manage that person or have absence-requests.manageAll. The overview lists every person (filters: year, business_function_id, operational_site_id, search) and can be exported to a file. Allowances are written through absence-allowances.',
        'absence-requests' => 'Absence requests (Assenze): a person\'s full-day or hourly absence of an absence type (absence_type_id, user_id), with one optional attachment. Flow draft -> submitted -> approved/rejected, or cancelled; approvers (superiors, else function managers, else HR) are snapshotted on submit and notified at each step; bulk decisions supported. Preview/insight give duration, balance and absent colleagues. To approve: POST /api/tables/absence-requests-to-approve/rows.',
        'absence-types' => 'Absence types (Tipi di assenza): HR catalogue of absence kinds, with flags for balance deduction, required approval, allowed granularity (full day, half day, hourly), minimum notice days, badge color and default annual days. Referenced by absence requests (absence_type_id); a type in use cannot be deleted (409), deactivate it instead. for-select returns the active types with their rule flags.',
        'absences' => 'Absences (Assenze), read-only views: GET calendar lists who is absent day by day in a from/to range (optional business_function_id), limited to the people the caller may see (own team or everyone); GET summary returns the caller counters (requests to approve, own pending), upcoming absences and who is absent today. The requests themselves live under /api/absence-requests.',
        'account-statements' => 'Read-only treasury reports for the account statement (Estratto conto): the balance of every financial account at a date, optionally for one company_id, with the total, and the receivable/payable installment collections and payments not assigned to any financial account. The statement of one account and its xlsx export are under /api/financial-accounts/{id}/statement.',
        'activity-log' => 'Activity log (Cronologia attività): the read-only change history of one record and its related records, for resources registered for it (e.g. leads, companies, contracts). GET /api/activity-log/{resource}/{id} uses cursor pagination (per_page, cursor) and an optional event filter (created/updated). It requires {resource}.viewActivity plus view on the record, and hides fields you may not see.',
        'addresses' => 'Addresses: postal addresses owned polymorphically (addressable_type/addressable_id; today the personal-data card behind registries and referents). Each has line1, line2, postal code, site type, geo ids (city_id, province_id, state_id, country_id), coordinates and is_primary. CRUD on single addresses, authorized through the owner resource.',
        'agent-fiscal-profiles' => 'Agent fiscal profiles (Profili fiscali): dated withholding-tax and ENASARCO settings of an agent referent (referent_id), with default vat_rate_id, payment_method_id and cost_type_id, valid from valid_from to valid_until (null = open-ended). Periods of the same referent cannot overlap (422); a profile used by a commission settlement cannot be deleted (409).',
        'agent-sales-report' => 'Agent sales report (Report Vendite Agenti): read-only report over quotes (offers), limited to the quotes the actor may see, with registry, category and commission data. These endpoints return synchronous xlsx downloads for the grid state: "details" (one block per offer with its revenue lines and commission/net totals) and "lines" (one flat row per revenue line); the summary is the generic POST /api/exports/agent-sales-report.',
        'ai-assistant' => 'AI assistant (Assistente AI): per-user chat conversations with a configured LLM provider (Anthropic or OpenAI-compatible). Sending a message streams the answer as server-sent events; a message may mention records of supported modules (module key + id), attach files and pass the current page guide. Config tells the UI which surfaces are enabled; other endpoints answer 404 while the assistant is off. Requires ai-assistant.use.',
        'api-clients' => 'External API integration clients (API e integrazioni): each client gets a technical user and a key (a Sanctum token) shown in plain text only on create and rotate-key, plus is_active, expires_at and a per-minute rate limit; deleting a client revokes its tokens. Also serves this API documentation as OpenAPI or Postman, regenerated only by docs/refresh (async, 202: poll docs/status).',
        'assignment' => 'Assignment helper for operator pickers (read-only; POST because it takes a selection body): for a domain (import_rows, leads, quotes, enrollees) and a selection of ids or an AG Grid select-all, returns the required competence categories, the shared operational site (Sede), the campaigns spanned and whether one operator can take them all. Pass the result to GET /api/users/for-select (operational_site_id, competence_category_ids[]).',
        'attachments' => 'Attachments (Documenti): generic file storage linked to a polymorphic owner via attachable_type alias (e.g. opportunity, work_order, contract, task, registry, purchase_order, treasury_movement) and attachable_id, optionally grouped in a named collection. Upload is checked against server size/MIME allowlists; files can be listed per owner, downloaded or streamed inline for preview, and deleted with their binary.',
        'attributes' => 'Global catalogue of dynamic attributes (Attributi): typed fields (unique code, name, type from the custom-field type registry, options for enum types, relation_target for relation types, help text, placeholder) that are linked to product categories and become the category\'s attr.* columns, e.g. in request-management.',
        'auth' => 'Authentication with Sanctum Bearer tokens. client-login lets an external API client, calling with its own client key, sign in a QNet user by email and password. It returns a user token bound to that client, which expires (expires_at) and acts with that user\'s permissions. logout revokes the current token.',
        'authorization' => 'Authorization catalogues for role management (Ruoli), read-only: GET fields returns the per-resource field catalogue for the field-permission matrix (needs roles.create or roles.update); GET permission-catalogue returns the Area > Module tree of assignable permissions and fields, grouped like the navigation. Roles themselves are managed under /api/roles.',
        'availability' => 'Availability: a public, unauthenticated probe polled by the maintenance screen. It answers 200 when the application is available and 503 during maintenance (except for excluded users).',
        'bank-reconciliations' => 'Saved bank reconciliations (Riconciliazioni bancarie) of a financial account: the bank balance at a statement date, the reconciled balance (opening balance plus ticked statement rows) and the difference between them. They are listed, previewed and created under /api/financial-accounts/{id}/bank-reconciliations. This module only deletes one; any adjustment treasury movement it created is kept as a normal movement.',
        'business-functions' => 'Business functions (Funzioni aziendali): organisational units with a name, a type (business unit, business service or neither), an optional manager (user), member users, companies, operational sites and a parent/child hierarchy (no cycles). Referenced by purchase requests, work order workflow criteria and the org chart; use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'campaigns' => 'Marketing campaigns (Campagne): optionally linked to a project (project_id), with partner referent, source, operational site, geo, dates, budget and lead target. Code CMP-0001... is generated on create (next-code suggests it); a linked campaign inherits status and product lines from its project and its budget must fit the project remaining budget (422). Leads belong to campaigns: a campaign with leads cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'chart-accounts' => 'Chart of accounts entries (Piano dei conti): managerial groups (Mastro, with kind cost/revenue/financial) and accounts (Conto, under a group via parent_id, inheriting its kind), each with a unique code. Revenue sub-accounts live under revenue-types and cost sub-accounts under cost-types; the full tree is GET /api/chart-of-accounts/tree. Deleting an entry still in use returns 409.',
        'chart-of-accounts' => 'Chart of accounts (Piano dei conti): three-level managerial chart, group > account > sub-account (revenue, cost and treasury types). GET tree returns the whole chart, GET export downloads it as csv or xlsx, POST import uploads a file in the same layout as a dry-run preview or an all-or-nothing apply. Groups and accounts are edited under /api/chart-accounts, revenue sub-accounts under /api/revenue-types.',
        'cities' => 'Cities: read-only geographic reference data feeding the address cascade (countries -> states -> provinces -> cities). Returns cities of a province_id (preferred) or state_id, or a name lookup by search when no parent is given, ordered by name and paginated with offset; city ids are used by addresses and personal-data cards.',
        'commission-adjustments' => 'Manual commission adjustments (Rettifiche): signed ADJUSTMENT movements of the commission ledger owed to an agent (referent_id) for a company_id, with amount, date and notes. Standalone ones wait for the next settlement run; with a draft commission_settlement_id they are attached and the draft is recalculated; once the settlement is issued they are frozen (409). List: POST /api/tables/commission-accruals/rows.',
        'commission-configurations' => 'Commission rules (Configuratore Commissioni): a fixed amount or a percentage for a recipient role (commercial, reporter, supervisor, supplier), scoped to a product category branch, a product or one recipient, with priority, validity dates and ACTIVE/SUSPENDED status. The rules generate the commissions of quote lines. quote-impact previews which open quotes a rule would update; recalculate-quotes runs that update as a background job.',
        'commission-settlement-runs' => 'Launches of the agent commission settlement (Lanci): for a period, optionally filtered by company, agents (referent_ids), recipient roles and a minimum amount, a run creates one DRAFT commission settlement per agent/company pair with open accrued movements and records the skipped pairs with their reason. A run is read-only history after creation.',
        'commission-settlements' => 'Agent commission statements (Estratti) per agent (referent) and company, computed from the accrued movements with VAT, withholding and ENASARCO amounts. Flow: DRAFT (notes, recalculate, delete) -> issue (number per company/year) -> agent document registered -> approve, which links or creates the agent\'s supplier registry and creates the purchase invoice. An issued settlement can be cancelled with a reason, releasing its movements.',
        'companies' => 'Companies (Società aziendali): the group\'s own legal entities, each with a denomination, an optional VAT number and a single address. Plain CRUD. Company sites, offers, invoices, purchase requests and orders, financial accounts and employment contracts reference them by company_id. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'company-closures' => 'Company closures (Chiusure aziendali): holidays or collective leave (kind holiday/collective_leave, starts_on/ends_on), valid for all operational sites or for the given operational_site_ids. Single-day holidays can repeat yearly. Closures make days non-working in the personal work calendar. A collective leave (absence_type_id) automatically generates approved absences for the people it covers. Once a non-yearly closure has started, editing or deleting it returns 409.',
        'company-sites' => 'Company sites (Società sedi): the sites of a company (company_id), each with its own name, a personal-data card with contacts and one address, bank accounts (IBAN, primary flag), a logo and custom fields. One site can be promoted to default. Referenced by company_site_id on quotes, opportunities, purchase requests/orders and purchase invoices. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'contacts' => 'Contacts: one reachable channel (type phone, fax, email, pec or website, with label, is_primary and is_work) owned polymorphically through contactable_type/contactable_id (currently personal_data cards). Values are normalized on write, there is at most one primary per owner and type, and a phone already used by another record is rejected (422).',
        'contract-statuses' => 'Contract statuses (Stati Contratto): configurable working statuses of contracts (contract_status_id), with color, description, group (open, pending, closed_won, closed_lost), active flag and one exclusive default. The system rows (Da validare, Validato, Sospeso, Annullato, Disdetto) are pinned and cannot be deleted; the custom rows can be reordered. Deleting a status that a contract uses returns 409. Use for-select.',
        'contract-types' => 'Contract types (Tipologie contrattuali): HR catalogue of employment contract types (name, active flag, sort order), referenced by the contractual conditions of users (contract_type_id, see /api/users/{user}/employment-contracts). A type in use cannot be deleted (409), deactivate it instead. for-select resolves ids.',
        'contracts' => 'Contracts (Contratti): lifecycle data of an offer (quote_id) that reached a closed-won status; never created or deleted by hand, they are born and suspended automatically by the offer status. Actions: validate, change-status (contract_status_id), terminate (also closes or stops its work orders), reactivate, open/undo renewals, and programme work orders (Commesse) from the offer revenue lines, single, batch or across several contracts. for-select resolves ids.',
        'cost-types' => 'Cost types (Tipi di costo): configurable lookup classifying costs, with code, name, nature (direct = chargeable to a work order, indirect, general/overhead), color, active flag and display order (reorder endpoint), optionally placed under a chart account (chart_account_id); a type in use cannot be deleted. Referenced by purchase order/invoice lines, work order costs, treasury movements and products. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'countries' => 'Countries: read-only geo reference, every country ordered by name. First step of the address cascade country > state (GET /api/states?country_id=) > province > city.',
        'custom-fields' => 'Custom fields (Campi personalizzati): admin definitions of typed dynamic fields added to an entity (entity_type, e.g. companies): key, type, label, options for enum fields, relation_target for relation fields, validation, group/tab, indexing, active flag. GET entities lists the entities that accept custom fields, GET relation-targets the entities a relation can point to. entity_type, type and key become immutable once values are recorded (422).',
        'dashboard' => 'Dashboard: task counters for the home page, each with a count and total minutes: not completed, assigned to me, assigned by me (with those to validate), created by me and observed by me. Each counter matches the same filter on the tasks list. Requires tasks.viewAny.',
        'document-bundles' => 'Document bundles (Modelli documenti): named sets of files (attachments uploaded through /api/attachments on the document_bundle owner) that the work order email composer can attach in bulk. Deleting a bundle also removes its files; use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'document-layouts' => 'Document layouts (Layout): reusable block-based templates (header/body/footer config) for the documents generated by one module: quotes, invoices or purchase_orders, with one default per module. Beyond CRUD: the catalogue of {category.key} variables, layout images (logos, letterhead), clone, and a PDF preview rendered against a quote_id, invoice_id or purchase_order_id, or a sample. for-select is filtered by module.',
        'email-templates' => 'Reusable email templates (Modelli email): name, module (work_orders, invoices, purchase_orders), subject, sanitized HTML body with {category.key} placeholders, and an active flag. variables returns the placeholder catalogue of a module. The email composers turn a template into an editable draft (e.g. purchase-orders emails/render-template). Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'enasarco-parameters' => 'ENASARCO rates and ceilings per year (Parametri ENASARCO): total rate, agent share percent, single-firm and multi-firm ceilings, notes. They feed the ENASARCO contribution of agent commission settlements by the year of the settlement period end; a year used by an issued settlement cannot be deleted (409).',
        'enrollee-management' => 'Enrollee management (Gestione Iscritti): a work panel over offers (Offerte, quote ids) whose workflow status group is validated or closed_won. It works like Gestione Richieste but cannot create records. You can read and update the operative fields (saved on the quote or its opportunity) and delete the offer (the opportunity is kept). Bulk actions: assign the GA2 operator or the GA1 manager, transfer to another operational site. Also offers category tabs and your favourite tabs.',
        'exports' => 'Exports (Esporta dati): generic asynchronous export of any table domain, reproducing the grid state (columns, sort, filters) as csv or xlsx. Creating an export opens an ExportRun (processing) and queues a job; poll the run until completed/failed, then download the file. Requires the domain\'s export permission; runs are visible only to their owner.',
        'field-change-requests' => 'Field change requests (Richieste di modifica): a proposal to change one protected field of a record (today the source of request-management and enrollee-management records) by a user who cannot write it directly. Creation snapshots the current value and notifies the designated role; approve applies the value (409 if the field changed meanwhile), reject closes it; the requester is notified. for-record lists a record\'s requests.',
        'financial-accounts' => 'Financial accounts of a company (Gestione Conti): bank accounts, cards and cash boxes, with type, IBAN and card data. The card number is stored encrypted and only the audited card-number endpoint reveals it. A card is linked to a bank account, which cannot be deleted while it has cards. Also sets the opening balance, returns the statement with running balance (+ xlsx export), ticks statement rows and manages bank reconciliations; for-select resolves ids.',
        'identity' => 'Live, non-blocking duplicate check (Possibile duplicato) used by the registry and referent create forms: given a tax code, a VAT number and/or email/phone contacts, returns up to 5 existing users, registries (Anagrafiche) or referents holding them, with the matched channels. Allowed to actors who can create a registry or a referent.',
        'imports' => 'Imports (Importa lead / Importa richieste): CSV/XLSX import wizard for the leads and request-management domains, run by queued jobs: analyzing -> configuring (column/value mapping, dedup strategy, saved mapping templates) -> staging -> reviewing (edit rows, resolve duplicates, bulk-assign operator/products) -> confirm -> completed, optionally converting to opportunities; rejected rows downloadable. List: POST /api/tables/import-runs/rows.',
        'installment-compensations' => 'Installment compensations (Compensazioni): closing a receivable installment (invoice_installment_id) against a payable one (purchase_invoice_installment_id) of the same registry and company, on a date, with an optional residual mode (spread or new installment). Not money, so never on account statements; deleting it restores both installments. Candidates and history are under /api/registries/{registry}/compensation-candidates and /compensations.',
        'invoice-installments' => 'Invoice installments (Scadenze): the scheduled payments of active invoices (Fatture Attive). You can edit due_date and payment_method_code while an installment has no collection. You can record a collection (collected_amount, collected_at, financial_account_id) or clear it. A partial collection spreads the residual over later installments, creates a new installment or writes it off; clearing restores the previous plan. Several installments of one customer can be collected at once, all or nothing.',
        'invoice-tags' => 'Invoice tags (Tag fattura): an optional label on an active invoice (e.g. estimate/final), with color, description, active flag and a manual order (reorder). Deleting a tag that an invoice carries returns 409. Use for-select.',
        'invoices' => 'Active invoices (Fatture Attive): proforma or invoice documents issued from a proforma request, with customer (customer_registry_id), company, payment method, lines with VAT and revenue type, server-computed totals and installments. Editing rebalances open installments; deletion is refused (409) once collected. Also PDF, monthly summary, installment preview, external number registration and emails (drafts with PDF, payment reminders, queued send). Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'job-activities' => 'Job activities (Attività): HR catalogue of work activities (name, description) linked to job roles (Mansioni); the link is edited from the job-role side. An activity in use cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'job-roles' => 'Job roles (Mansioni): a catalogue of name and description, linked to job activities (job_activity_ids) and assigned to employees\' employment profiles; unrelated to the permission roles of /api/roles. Skills of the catalogue reference job roles with a minimum level, which drives the user-skills coverage view. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'leads' => 'Leads (Lead): contacts generated by a campaign. Each links a registry (registry_id, Anagrafiche) to a campaign_id, with optional operational_site_id, source_id, operator_id (Operatore), notes and extra_fields. Beyond CRUD: convert to an Opportunity (Opportunità) on create or in bulk, which also creates its offer; bulk-assign the operator; opportunity-defaults pre-fills an opportunity from a lead. Use for-select.',
        'management-control' => 'Management control (Controllo di gestione): read-only analytical reports filtered by period, company, company site and operational site: income statement (Conto economico), structure costs, receivables/payables exposure (Scadenzario ed esposizione), forecast cash flow, monthly trend (Andamento mensile), billing (Fatturazione), account flows (Conti) and agents ranking (Agenti). Requires management-control.view.',
        'meta' => 'Resource metadata: for a registered resource name, returns the field catalogue used by create forms (native fields plus custom-field descriptors with options/relations) and the actor\'s permissions block for that resource. Requires the resource\'s viewAny permission; unknown resources return 404.',
        'navigation' => 'Navigation: the backend-driven sidebar menu tree for the authenticated user, filtered by their permissions; optional ?workspace=<slug> restricts it to one App workspace (404 if unknown). Read-only.',
        'notes' => 'Notes (Note): collaborative discussion entries attached to a host record via entity_type (e.g. request-management, tasks, work-orders, proforma-requests, registries, referents, purchase-requests) and entity_id, with one level of replies (parent_id), optional quote scoping (quote_id), rich-text body and @mentions of users, who get a notification. Edits are tracked and deletion is soft. mentionable-users lists who can be mentioned.',
        'notifications' => 'Notifications (Notifiche): the authenticated user\'s own in-app notifications, produced by other modules (e.g. absence decisions, mentions, field change requests). Endpoints list them paginated, return the unread count with the latest unread item, and mark one, several or all as read (or one as unread). Foreign ids are ignored or 404.',
        'operational-sites' => 'Operational sites (Sedi operative): physical locations identified by their address (line1, city_id and the other geo ids), with an optional alias and an active flag. They scope leads, the offers of Gestione Richieste and Gestione Iscritti (operator assignment and transfers), personnel and company closures. Use for-select.',
        'opportunities' => 'Opportunities (Opportunità): a commercial deal for a client registry (registry_id, Anagrafiche), created by hand or converted from a lead (lead_id, one per lead; conversion also creates its offer), with referent, commercial, supervisor, product lines and estimated value. Status is computed from its offers (Offerte). Only one open opportunity per registry unless its categories allow several (422 with existing_opportunity_id); with offers, delete is 409. for-select resolves ids.',
        'org-chart' => 'Organisation chart (Organigramma) of active users and business functions: functions returns the function tree with their members (plus the people with no function), people returns each person with managers, job roles and functions. The move endpoints put a person under another manager, a function under another parent, or a person into another function, with validation and an activity log entry.',
        'payment-methods' => 'Payment methods (Modalità di Pagamento): catalogue of payment modalities with unique immutable code, fiscal payment_method_code (e.g. MP01), instructions and installment rules (payment days, installments count and spacing, end of month, excluded months, VAT allocation). Referenced via payment_method_id by offers, purchase orders and invoices, proforma requests; reorder sets the display order; a method in use cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'personal-data' => 'Personal data cards (Dati anagrafici): the identity sheet of a polymorphic owner (personable_type alias, today user, plus personable_id), one card per owner: individual (first/last name, tax code, birth data, gender) or company (company name, VAT number, SDI code), with nested contacts and addresses. Can be fetched by owner; deleting a card cascades its contacts and addresses.',
        'pipeline-statuses' => 'Statuses of projects and campaigns (Stati progetto/campagna): name, color, group (open, pending, closed) and order; the system rows Nuovo and Chiuso are protected. reorder resequences the custom rows; a status referenced by a project or campaign cannot be deleted (409). Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'product-categories' => 'Product categories (Categorie Prodotto): an unlimited-depth tree (parent_id) classifying products. Attributes per context (product, quote, work_order) are inherited from ancestors. Each category has business_function_id, revenue_type_id, manager labels and flags that drive offers, contracts and Gestione Richieste. Beyond CRUD: the full tree, all-or-nothing bulk-move, duplicate with layouts, attribute layouts, effective attributes and manager labels, report columns. Use for-select.',
        'product-category-branches' => 'Product category branches: for-select only. It returns the product categories that have at least one child, selectable or not, for the branch criterion of the offer status configurator (Configuratore Stati Offerta).',
        'product-category-nodes' => 'Read-only picker of every active product category (Categorie Prodotto), containers included and is_selectable ignored, as paged {id, label}: used by the commission configurator, where a category rule covers the whole branch. Categories themselves are managed in the product-categories module.',
        'product-category-roots' => 'Product category roots: read-only for-select of the first-level (parent) product categories, used to resolve the "Categoria madre" filter ids; with actor_roots, an actor limited to some parent categories gets only those.',
        'product-typologies' => 'Product typologies (Tipologie Prodotto): a classification of products with code (immutable after create), name, description and color, plus a supplier_commission_enabled flag and an optional proforma_kind (consultancy/institution). Deletion is refused while products use the typology. Use for-select.',
        'products' => 'Products (Prodotti): catalogue items with code (PRD-0001... generated when not given; next-code suggests it), category, cost and price, VAT rate, unit of measure, typology, default cost and revenue types, usages (SALE/COST/INTERNAL: which offer tab may pick it), suppliers and category attribute values. Bulk endpoints set activation, cost type or revenue type; supplier-commissions tells which suppliers carry a commission on a product. for-select accepts category_ids[].',
        'proforma-requests' => 'Proforma requests (Richieste Proforma): a request to Accounting to bill a work order (work_order_id, quote_id), either its consultancy lines or one supplier institution lines (kind). Created via POST /api/work-orders/{workOrder}/proforma-requests; only the note is editable. invoice-draft prefills and POST invoice issues the active invoice (Fatture Attive), moving the request from pending to issued; issued or invoiced requests cannot be deleted (409).',
        'projects' => 'Projects (Progetti): marketing projects grouping campaigns (Campagne), with code PRJ-0001... (generated; next-code suggests it), pipeline status, product lines, geo, partner referent, operational site, dates, total budget and lead target; linked campaigns inherit status and product lines and draw on its budget. GET /api/projects is a paginated card list with campaign and lead counts, summary gives KPI totals. A project with campaigns cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'provinces' => 'Provinces: read-only geographic reference data. GET /api/provinces?state_id= lists the provinces of a state (the filter is required); for-select is the free-search picker. Addresses reference them as province_id.',
        'purchase-invoice-installments' => 'Payment schedule installments of purchase invoices (Scadenze passive): view and edit due date and payment method, record or clear the payment of one installment (amount, date, financial account; a partial payment spreads the residual, adds a new installment or writes it off), or pay several installments of one supplier at once. Requires the pay ability on the parent purchase invoice.',
        'purchase-invoices' => 'Purchase invoices (Fatture passive): payable documents of a supplier to a company, a proforma until the supplier document number is set, then a registered invoice. Lines can come from purchase orders (ODA; see invoiceable-orders and draft); amounts and the installment schedule are computed server-side (installment-preview). Full edit only on a proforma, rebalanced once payments exist; PATCH details sets number and notes; an invoice or a document with payments cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'purchase-order-statuses' => 'Purchase order statuses (Stati ODA): presentation catalogue of the fixed purchase order status enum (draft, in_validation, approved, sent_to_supplier, partially_fulfilled, fulfilled, cancelled): only name, badge color, icon and display order can be edited or reordered; rows are never created or deleted and drive no logic. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'purchase-orders' => 'Purchase orders (ODA) to a supplier registry for a company, with lines (product, cost type, quantity, price, VAT, work order) and optional work order, quote and opportunity links; numbered per company/year, optionally created as monthly copies. Status flow: draft, in_validation, approved, sent_to_supplier, partially_fulfilled/fulfilled or cancelled. Also merge, PDF, supplier emails with the PDF attached, delivery receipts, residual closing; for-select.',
        'purchase-request-line-statuses' => 'Purchase request line statuses (Stati righe RDA): the display catalogue of the fixed line statuses of purchase requests (pending_approval, approved, ordered, received, rejected, on_hold). There is one system row per status and no create or delete; only name, color and icon can change, and the rows can be reordered. Use for-select.',
        'purchase-request-lines' => 'Purchase request lines (Gestione righe RDA): lines of purchase requests (RDA) with product, supplier, quantity, price and status (pending_approval, approved, rejected, on_hold, ordered, received). Bulk endpoints change status (all-or-nothing, per-request role checks, logged, auto-closing finished requests), set suppliers, and generate draft purchase orders (ODA) from approved lines, one per supplier/company/site group. status-logs returns a line history.',
        'purchase-request-priorities' => 'Purchase request priorities (Priorità RDA): configurable priority levels of purchase requests (RDA), with color, icon, description, active and default flags and a manual order (reorder). Deleting a priority that a purchase request uses returns 409. Use for-select.',
        'purchase-requests' => 'Purchase requests (RDA) for a company and business function, with priority, optional customer and work order, and lines (product, supplier, quantity, price, VAT) moving through pending_approval, approved, rejected, on_hold, ordered, received. The function manager is notified (in-app and email) on creation and via notify-manager; approver-options lists eligible approvers; close ends the request (forced: reason). Lines: POST /api/tables/purchase-request-lines/rows; for-select.',
        'quote-offer-lines' => 'Offer lines, for-select only: the revenue lines of one offer (quote_id required), searchable by product code or name, excluding lines already programmed into another work order in the same renewal period (except_work_order_id keeps those of the work order being edited). Used to pick the lines of a work order (Commessa); requires work-orders.view or quotes.view.',
        'quote-workflows' => 'Offer workflows (Configuratore Stati Offerta): activatable sets of matching criteria (product category, business function, source, opportunity custom relation fields; see criterion-fields) with their own offer statuses (color, group open/pending/validated/closed_won/closed_lost, requires_note). Each offer (Offerta) takes the workflow its data matches, else the global default status set (default-statuses). Criteria combinations are unique; a workflow whose statuses are still used by offers cannot be deleted (409).',
        'quotes' => 'Quotes (Offerte): commercial offers under an opportunity (opportunity_id), with generated code (QUO-0001), workflow status (quote_workflow_status_id), commercial/reporter referents, supervisor, company, sites, payment method, revenue and cost lines with agent commissions and dynamic attributes; totals are recalculated server-side. Also .docx generation and commission recalculation; a quote with work orders cannot be deleted. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'referent-types' => 'Referent types (Tipi referente): simple name-only lookup classifying referents (referent_type_id); a type in use cannot be deleted. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'referents' => 'Referents (Referenti): internal or external contact persons/entities with a personal-data card (contacts, addresses), an optional type (referent_type_id), linked user account (user_id) and supplier registry the agent is paid through (supplier_registry_id). Used as commercial/reporter on opportunities and quotes and as commission recipients. rewards returns the referent\'s rewards (rewarded-referents module). Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'registries' => 'Customer and supplier records (Anagrafiche): a personal-data card (name, tax code, VAT number, contacts, addresses) plus is_supplier, source, sectors, referents with a primary one, internal managers, commercial/reporter referents, supervisor user, agreement and size data. Also the ledger (Partitario: customer and supplier sections) and the receivable/payable installment compensations of the registry. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'request-management' => 'Request management (Gestione Richieste): operational work panel where each row is an offer (quote id). Create builds registry (if new), opportunity and offer at once (form-context returns extra fields per category); update writes operative fields onto the offer or its opportunity. Bulk actions assign the GA2 operator or GA1 manager or transfer requests to another operational site, within the caller scope. Also category tabs, an async statistics report (create, poll, download) and a dashboard.',
        'revenue-types' => 'Revenue sub-accounts (Sottoconti di ricavo) of the management chart of accounts (Piano dei conti): code and name under a revenue account (chart_account_id). Invoice lines, products and product categories reference them as revenue_type_id; at most one is flagged as the institution-commission default. Deletable only while unused. They appear in GET /api/chart-of-accounts/tree. Use for-select.',
        'reward-statuses' => 'Reward statuses (Stati Buoni Collegati): ordered, coloured statuses of an assigned voucher/reward (reward_status_id), each in group pending, closed_won or closed_lost. The system rows (In attesa, Approvato, Negato) and any status used by a reward cannot be deleted (409); reorder resequences the custom rows. for-select resolves ids.',
        'reward-types' => 'Reward types (Buoni, Premi e Incentivi): catalogue of voucher, reward and incentive types (unique name, color) used by the rewards assigned to referents (reward_type_id). A type in use cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'rewards' => 'Rewards: a voucher, prize or incentive of a reward type (Buoni, Premi e Incentivi) assigned to a referent (referent_id), originating from an opportunity. Rewards are created and edited only through the opportunity / Gestione Richieste payload. This endpoint only changes their status by hand (reward_status_id, Stati Buoni Collegati) and requires rewarded-referents.update. List: POST /api/tables/rewarded-referents/rows.',
        'roles' => 'Permission roles (Ruoli): a unique name, the permission names it grants and the user ids holding it (Spatie roles). The system super-admin role cannot be modified or deleted (422). Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'sectors' => 'Sectors (Settori): an unlimited-depth tree of code and name with an active flag (an inactive node deactivates its whole subtree), used to classify registries (sector_ids). tree returns the nested tree, roots first; a sector cannot be moved under itself or a descendant. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'skills' => 'Skills (Catalogo competenze): catalogue of skills (name, optional category, description, active flag) assigned to people in the user-skills module; a skill in use cannot be deleted and is deactivated instead. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'sources' => 'Sources (Fonti): a name-only catalogue of where a contact or request comes from. Registries, leads, campaigns and offers reference it as source_id. Deletion is refused while a lead or campaign uses it. Use for-select.',
        'staff-courses' => 'Staff courses (Corsi): catalogue of internal training courses for employees (name, description, duration_minutes, validity_months, active flag), unrelated to courses sold to customers. Job roles may require courses and staff trainings (Formazione) reference them; a course in use cannot be deleted (409), deactivate it instead. for-select resolves ids.',
        'staff-trainings' => 'Staff trainings (Formazione): a register of courses (staff_course_id, Corsi) taken by a person (user_id), with completed_on, outcome passed/failed and an expires_on derived from the course validity, plus one optional certificate file. The compliance view crosses people with the courses their job roles (Mansioni) require: valid, expiring, expired or missing. Writes need staff-trainings.manage.',
        'states' => 'States/regions: read-only geo reference. GET /api/states?country_id= lists the states of a country (address cascade, then provinces and cities); GET states/for-select is a searchable paginated picker limited to the national country, with ids[] hydration.',
        'stats' => 'Statistics panel (Statistiche) of a module: GET /api/stats/{domain} returns the cached widgets of a domain registered in config/stats.php (e.g. registries, referents, companies, products, projects, campaigns, leads, opportunities, quotes, tasks, users). An unknown domain is 404; it requires the domain\'s viewAny permission.',
        'stock-balances' => 'Stock balances (Dotazioni): read-only quantities of tracked products (equipment) per operational site, either free or assigned to a user, optionally filtered by product_id, user_id, operational_site_id. Balances change only through append-only stock movements (POST /api/stock-movements).',
        'stock-movements' => 'Append-only stock and equipment register (Magazzino e Dotazioni): LOAD, UNLOAD, TRANSFER between operational sites, ASSIGN/RETURN of items to a user and ADJUSTMENT to a counted quantity, for a product_id at an operational_site_id; movements are never edited or deleted. GET returns the history of one product at one site (optionally one user). Balances: POST /api/tables/stock-balances/rows.',
        'support-requests' => 'Support requests (Assistenza tecnica): any authenticated user can report an IT problem by choosing an active support topic and describing it (urgent flag, attachments, page URL and browser). The request is turned into a Task whose type, category, priority, importance, assignees, watchers and deadline come from the topic configuration. topics lists the selectable topics.',
        'support-topics' => 'Problem types of IT support requests (Assistenza tecnica): name, icon, order, active flag and the settings of the Task a user\'s request becomes (task type, category, priority and urgent priority, importance, due days, assignees, watchers, private, closure feedback). Users submit requests via POST /api/support-requests, which creates the Task.',
        'tables' => 'Generic server-side list framework behind every grid: for a table domain (e.g. registries, purchase-orders, tasks) it returns the column schema with the user\'s saved layout, paged rows with filters, sort and search (AG Grid SSRM), distinct values for set filters, inline cell edits, best-effort bulk delete, persisted filters/layout and named filter views (own or shared, favorites). Authorization is the domain\'s viewAny plus per-row/field checks. See the guide at the top of this document.',
        'tags' => 'Tags (Tag): a name-only classification lookup, currently not attached to other records. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'task-categories' => 'Task categories (Categorie Task): a nested (parent_id) classification of tasks with color, icon, description, active flag and a manual order (reorder). Deleting a category that a task uses returns 409. Use for-select.',
        'task-importances' => 'Task importances (Importanza Task): configurable lookup for tasks (task_importance_id) with name, description, badge color/icon, display order (reorder endpoint), active and default flags. Deleting an importance used by a task returns 409. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'task-priorities' => 'Task priorities (Priorità Task): configurable priority lookup for tasks (name, description, color and icon tokens, sort order, active and default flags), referenced via task_priority_id. reorder resequences the rows; a priority used by a task cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'task-statuses' => 'Task statuses (Stati Task): name, color, icon, phase group (open, pending, in_validation, closed_positive, closed_negative) and completion percentage, which sets the progress of every task in that status. The protected system rows cannot be deleted (422), nor a status used by a task (409); reorder changes the display order. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'task-templates' => 'Task templates (Modelli di Task): reusable sets of task rows (items) organized in stages and up to 3 nested levels, each with initial status, attachments and an optional work order status to move to when closed; items are written only inside the template create/update as a full sync. Work orders use a template to generate their tasks; a template used by a work order cannot be deleted. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'task-types' => 'Task types (Tipologie Task): a classification of tasks with color, icon, description, active and default flags, a manual order (reorder) and requires_time_entry: when set, completing a task of that type requires a time entry (Segnatempo). Deleting a type that a task uses returns 409. Use for-select.',
        'tasks' => 'Tasks (Task): hierarchical activities (parent_task_id) linkable to registry, referent, lead, opportunity and work order (Commessa) stage, with type, status, priority, importance, category, dates, assignees, watchers, optional recurrence and privacy. Actions: complete/uncomplete, approve/reject when validation is required, block/unblock, request-update, sub-task reorder, bulk actions and time entries (Segnatempo). Changes notify involved users; deleting a task deletes its whole sub-task tree, refused when one of them cannot be deleted.',
        'time-entries' => 'Time entries (Segnatempo): time logged by a user on a date (start/end or minutes, task type), optionally linked to a registry, opportunity, work order, work order stage or task (a task imposes its title and links). Offers the day dashboard, per-day notes, overview/pulse/team statistics and synchronous xlsx exports (filtered and monthly). Users see their own entries; managing others\' requires manageAll.',
        'treasury-movements' => 'Treasury movements (Movimenti di tesoreria): manual movements on a financial account (financial_account_id): income, expense, transfer to another account of the same company (counterpart_account_id) or balance adjustment (direction), with a positive amount, date, description and one classification (cost_type_id, revenue_type_id or treasury_type_id), optionally linked to a registry and a work order.',
        'treasury-overview' => 'Treasury overview (Quadro finanziario): read-only financial snapshot at today, optionally for one company (company_id): liquidity by financial account, receivable and payable totals with overdue ageing, net position, forecast, and items to verify (unassigned, adjustments, unreconciled).',
        'treasury-types' => 'Financial sub-accounts (Sottoconti finanziari) of the chart of accounts (Piano dei conti): code, name and active flag under a financial account (chart_account_id). They classify treasury movements (Movimenti di tesoreria, treasury_type_id) and can be deleted only while no movement uses them. They appear in GET /api/chart-of-accounts/tree. Use for-select.',
        'units-of-measure' => 'Units of measure (Unità di Misura): lookup of units (unique immutable code, name, symbol, description) qualifying the quantities of products and offer lines (unit_of_measure_id); products default to the unit with code unit. A unit in use cannot be deleted (409). for-select resolves ids.',
        'user-skills' => 'Skills held by people (Competenze): one row per user and skill (Catalogo competenze) with level 1-4 (basic to expert), assessment date, assessor and notes; level changes stay in the activity log. Reads follow the actor\'s visibility scope (a manager sees subordinates), writes need manage. coverage returns, per person, the skills required by their job roles at the highest minimum level.',
        'users' => 'Users (Utenti): application accounts with roles, active flag, preferences, personal-data card, employment profile and avatar. Create generates a password and emails a welcome message (resend-welcome reissues it with a forced change); roles are limited to those the caller may assign. bulk-activation toggles many users; employment-contracts holds the dated contractual conditions. Delete is 409 for the last super-admin or a user still referenced. for-select filters by operational_site_id and competence_category_ids[].',
        'vat-rates' => 'VAT rates (IVA): lookup of VAT percentages (name, rate) referenced by products and by quote, invoice, purchase request/order and purchase invoice lines (vat_rate_id). A rate in use cannot be deleted. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'work-order-payment-statuses' => 'Work order payment statuses (Stati pagamento commessa): configurable lookup for the payment status of work order lines, with name, description, color, active flag, display order (reorder endpoint) and allows_delivery; moving a line to an allows_delivery status notifies the work order participants that it can be delivered. Deleting a status still used returns 409. Use for-select to resolve ids.',
        'work-order-workflow-statuses' => 'Work order workflow statuses: for-select only. It returns every status of every work order workflow (Configuratore Stati Commessa) plus the default set, for picking a status in task template rows (Modelli di Task).',
        'work-order-workflows' => 'Status workflows for work orders (Configuratore Stati Commessa): named sets of criteria that can be switched on or off (business function, product category or category branch, matched on the work order\'s revenue lines), each with its own status list (system rows plus custom ones). Work orders that match no workflow use the global default status set (default-statuses). criterion-fields lists the allowed fields; a workflow whose statuses are still in use cannot be deleted (409).',
        'work-orders' => 'Work orders (Commesse): jobs created from an offer (quote_id, Offerte) and its revenue quote_line_ids. Each gets a COM-0001 code (next-code previews it), supervisors, a workflow status and an optional task_template_id that generates its tasks. The open/completed/closed status is computed from progress entries or a forced close. Sub-resources: stages and task board, emails (send, schedule), costs, contract data and line payments, proforma requests, invoices, project chat, request-update. Use for-select.',
        'workspaces' => 'Workspaces (App): named subsets of the navigation menu (slug, name, description, icon, color, sort order, navigation_keys). available returns, for any user, the workspaces whose menu is not empty for their permissions, with their home route. CRUD and the navigation catalogue are super-admin only.',
    ];
}
